\ sync.fam — a fast sync from a peer (docs/NODE.md, step 6), and the
\ relay of transactions (step 7), after p2p.fam.
\ As tabminer's node.rs: headers first, each checked but for its proof of
\ work in full (the quick check from its claimed mix); then the block S a
\ depth below the best, the full proof of work of the best header (hconf),
\ S's body and its snapshot's manifest, S's chain proof (which covers
\ every block before it, their work too), the snapshot's parts, the state
\ checked whole; then the blocks after S, each connected with its proof
\ checked, which attests to its parent's work (docs/NODE.md, the work in
\ the chain proof).  So every header's work is checked: the best's
\ directly, each other's by a verified proof (S's by S+1's, and so on).
\ None needs its own full check but the best, which no proof covers.  Then the tip followed: each block a peer announces (Inv), its
\ header checked in full, fetched and connected.
\
\ nsync ( depth -- code )  0, or where it stopped: -1 no Pong, -2 another
\ genesis, -3 headers refused or not coming, -4 a proof of work, -5 a
\ block or manifest not fetched, -6 S's proof, -7 a part, -8 the state,
\ -9 a block after S.
\ pfollow ( n -- k )  the tip followed until n more blocks are connected
\ (a minute each at most): on each announcement (Inv), the headers and
\ blocks missing fetched and connected (ncatch), so one missed costs
\ nothing.  How many.
\ ntime ( -- s )  the date (/proc/time).
\ nrelay  each announced transaction not pooled fetched from its peer and
\ offered to the pool (a line "pool: code id" for each); if pooled,
\ announced to the other peers.
\ nserve ( s -- )  s seconds of following the tip and relaying.

: nbuf variable ;  : nS variable ;  : nH variable ;  : ncode variable ;  : nid variable ;
: nblk variable ;  : nbn variable ;  : nk variable ;

: nfail  ncode @ 0= if ncode ! else drop then ;   \ ( code -- )

\ nstat  our status from the state: the tip's height and id, its work.
: nstat
stfd @ 0 lit txbegin stx !  62 lit mget myold !  68 lit mget  stx @ txcommit drop  dup myh !
\ the oldest body kept: the first, or the window's (1,008) start
myold @ if myh @ 3EF lit - myold @ max myh @ 3EF lit u< if drop myold @ then myold ! then
hat dup hid mytip @ 8 lit wcopy  hwork mywork @ 8 lit wcopy ;

\ nfetch ( kind part id -- a n | 0 0 )  pfetch, the API answered while it
\ fetches: each time a connection waits, pfetch stops (pyld), the API
\ answers it (in transactions of its own: stx kept, as vwait does) and
\ the waiting requests whose tip moved, and the fetch goes on.
: nfkd variable ;  : nfpt variable ;  : nfid variable ;  : nfsv variable ;
: nfetch
nfid ! nfpt ! nfkd !
begin
	-1 lit pyld !  nfkd @ nfpt @ nfid @ pfetch  0 lit pyld !
	over 0= pyd @ and
while
	2drop  stx @ nfsv !  aaccept awake  nfsv @ stx !
repeat ;

\ nidle ( s -- )  s seconds of serving only: peers' requests (pwait; each
\ peer pinged when its time comes, pkeep) and the API; nothing fetched.
\ For a node waiting to sync (main.fam): no peer yet, or none ahead.
: nidt variable ;
: nidle
secs + nidt !
begin secs nidt @ u< while
	-1 lit pxw !  3B9ACA00 lit pwait drop  0 lit pxw !  pkeep  stx @ nfsv !  aaccept awake  nfsv @ stx !
repeat ;

\ nblock ( e -- flag )  the block of entry e fetched into nblk/nbn (its
\ header the entry's: the bytes the same).
: nft variable ;  : btf variable ;
: nwhy variable ;
: nblock
ticks nft !  1 lit nwhy !
1 lit pact !  dup 20 lit + @ pacth !
dup hid 0 lit 0 lit rot nfetch nbn ! nblk !  0 lit pact !
nblk @ if
	nbn @ CC lit u< 0= if nblk @ swap hhdr CC lit d8= dup 0= if 3 lit nwhy ! then else drop 2 lit nwhy ! 0 lit then
	dup 0= if nblk @ free 0 lit nblk ! then
else drop 0 lit then
ticks nft @ - btf ! ;
\ The next block fetched while the worker connects this one: the loops
\ that connect blocks set npnx to the next block's entry before nconnect,
\ which, once the worker has the job, fetches that block (npfetch) into
\ npb/npn (npe its entry) while it waits; nbget then takes it rather than
\ fetching it again.  The fetch is the network's time (a round trip a
\ window of chunks), the connection the worker's: so they overlap.
\ npk: the peer to fetch it from, plus one (0: the current); npks the
\ peer it came from.
: npk variable ;  : npks variable ;  : npsv variable ;
\ nsil: the peers (a bit each, by index) that sent nothing when asked for
\ a block in this run (nrun): not asked again in it, rather than once
\ for each block the batch is still missing.
: nsil variable ;
: nsil?  1 lit swap lshift nsil @ and 0= 0= ;   \ ( k -- flag )
: nsil!  1 lit swap lshift nsil @ or nsil ! ;   \ ( k -- )
: nsvt variable ;  : npnx variable ;  : npe variable ;  : npb variable ;  : npn variable ;  : nsvb variable ;  : nsvn variable ;
\ npdrop  a block fetched ahead and not used, dropped.
: npdrop  npb @ ?dup if free then  0 lit npb !  0 lit npe ! ;
\ npfetch  npnx's block fetched into npb/npn, nblk and nbn kept.
: npfetch
npnx @ ?dup if
	npdrop  nblk @ nsvb !  nbn @ nsvn !
	pcur @ dup npsv ! npks !  npk @ ?dup if 1 lit - dup npks ! puse then
	dup nblock if npe !  nblk @ npb !  nbn @ npn ! else drop  nwhy @ 1 lit = if npks @ nsil! then then
	npk @ if npsv @ puse then
	nsvb @ nblk !  nsvn @ nbn !
then
0 lit npnx !  0 lit npk ! ;
\ nbget ( e -- flag )  entry e's block into nblk/nbn: the one fetched ahead
\ if it is e's (its fetch then took no time here), else fetched now.
: nbget
dup npe @ =  npb @ 0= 0= and if
	drop  npb @ nblk !  npn @ nbn !  0 lit npb !  0 lit npe !  0 lit btf !  -1 lit
else npdrop nblock then ;
\ nwhy.  why the last block was not fetched.
: nwhy.
nwhy @ 1 lit = if " (nothing came)" else nwhy @ 2 lit = if " (too short to hold a header)" else
" (its header is not the one held: another block came)" then then puts ;

\ nsay ( s -- )  "node: s", if vrb.
: nsay  vrb @ if nhead puts else drop then ;
\ nsec ( ticks -- )  as seconds, to the hundredth.
: nsec  2710 lit / dup 3E8 lit / u. 2E lit putc 3E8 lit % A lit / dup A lit u< if 30 lit putc then u. ;
\ nbrk  what the last block took, by part (sconnect's btb...).
: nbrk
"  (fetch " puts btf @ nsec  ", body " puts btb @ nsec  ", state " puts bts @ nsec  ", proof " puts btp @ nsec
", store " puts btc @ nsec  "; " puts btf @ btb @ + bts @ + btp @ + btc @ + nsec " s)" puts ;
: nt0 variable ;  : nh0 variable ;
: nsayn  vrb @ if u. 0A lit putc else drop then ;   \ ( n -- )  a number ending the line

\ The verifier, nodev (vmain.fam): a process of its own running a
\ header's full proof of work and a block's chain proof while the node
\ serves.  vinit starts it (its 0 reading the jobs' pipe, its 1 writing
\ the verdicts'); vjw is 0 if it could not be, or once it is gone: the
\ checks then run here, as before.  vwait serves the network while it
\ works (Pings, peers, headers, images, pooled transactions; not blocks'
\ chunks, which share the store's transaction a block's connection may
\ hold open: pnest) and the API.
\ nnet: the network (0 mainnet, 1 the recursive dev network: main.fam's
\ -n), whose verifier nodev loads.
: nnet variable ;
: vjw variable ;  : vjr variable ;  : vwk variable ;  : vp1 variable ;  : vp2 variable ;  : vfds variable ;  : vsav variable ;
\ vput ( a n -- )  bytes to nodev; a write that fails, it gone (vjw 0).
: vput
begin dup vjw @ 0= 0= and while
	vjw @ 2 lit pick 2 lit pick write
	dup 0 lit > if rot over + -rot - else drop 0 lit vjw ! then
repeat 2drop ;
: vw  vwk @ !  vwk @ 4 lit vput ;                 \ ( x -- )  a word to nodev
: vinit
0 lit vjw !  10 lit alloc vwk !  10 lit alloc vp1 !  10 lit alloc vp2 !  10 lit alloc vfds !
vp1 @ pipe 0< 0=  vp2 @ pipe 0< 0= and if
	2 lit vfds @ !  vp1 @ @ vfds @ 4 lit + !  vp2 @ 4 lit + @ vfds @ 8 lit + !
	"nodev" 0 lit vfds @ spawnv 0< if
		vp1 @ @ close drop  vp1 @ 4 lit + @ close drop  vp2 @ @ close drop  vp2 @ 4 lit + @ close drop
	else
		vp1 @ 4 lit + @ vjw !  vp2 @ @ vjr !
		vp1 @ @ close drop  vp2 @ 4 lit + @ close drop
		0 lit vw  pwitems @ vw  pwpar @ vw  pwacc @ vw  nnet @ vw
	then
then ;
\ vwait ( -- flag | -2 )  nodev's verdict, the network served meanwhile,
\ and the API (its requests read the store in transactions of their own:
\ stx, which a block's connection may hold, kept for it); -2 if nodev is
\ gone (the caller checks here).
: vwait
vjr @ pyfd !  0 lit pyrdy !  1 lit pnest !
begin vjw @ if pyrdy @ 0= else 0 lit then while
	-1 lit pxw !  3B9ACA00 lit pwait drop  0 lit pxw !
	\ the peers kept (pings) and the API's long polls answered meanwhile
	pkeep
	stx @ vsav !  pxrdy @ if aaccept then  awake  vsav @ stx !
repeat
0 lit pyfd !  0 lit pyrdy !  0 lit pnest !
vjw @ if
	vjr @ vwk @ 4 lit read 4 lit = if vwk @ @ else 0 lit vjw ! FFFFFFFE lit then
else FFFFFFFE lit then ;
\ vpow ( e -- flag )  entry e's full proof of work against htg (its target).
: vpow
vjw @ if 1 lit vw  dup CC lit vput  htg @ 20 lit vput  vwait else FFFFFFFE lit then
dup FFFFFFFE lit = if drop htg @ fullpow else nip then ;
\ vproof ( -- flag )  the chain proof of the block sconn1 left (ppub, bpr).
: vproof
vjw @ if 2 lit vw  ppub @ 40 lit vput  bnpr @ vw  bpr @ bnpr @ vput  vwait else FFFFFFFE lit then
dup FFFFFFFE lit = if drop ppub @ bpr @ bnpr @ cvverify then ;
\ The worker: a thread with variables of its own (pthread, docs/OS.md)
\ that connects and undoes blocks (sconnect, its chain proof checked
\ there too, and sundo), the store's writes and commit with them, while
\ the node serves (cwait: peers, the API).  It shares nothing with the
\ node but the job (cwj, from malloc) and the store: the node only reads
\ the chain's tree meanwhile (its own transactions, as of the last
\ commit), and writes it only while the worker is idle.  cwinit makes its
\ own buffers (sconnect's and sundo's, found by tracing what they reach)
\ but for the tables that are only read (the squares, dflt's empty
\ subtrees, the chain's constants, the verifier's program, genesis's
\ mix).  Jobs come on a pipe (a word: 1 connect, 2 undo), their verdict
\ back on another.  If it cannot be started (cwon 0) the work is done
\ here, as before.
\ Besides, a fast sync's snapshot: its manifest (3: snman, the parts'
\ count back at +24), S's chain proof (5: sverify), each part (6:
\ snpart), the whole (7: snfin); the snapshot's state is then the
\ worker's, from the manifest to the last part.
\ cwj: +0 the header entry (or the first argument), +4 the body (the
\ second), +8 its length (the third), +C sprchk, +10 the store (stfd),
\ +14 to +20 the times (btb, bts, btp, btc), +24 the parts' count, +28
\ to +34 what a connected block leaves for the pool (qconfs, qmvblk):
\ bout (in the body, the node's), bnout, sfirst, sfirsth; +38 and +3C the
\ counter before a block (lo, hi) and +40 its parent's header, for its
\ proof checked early (9: sbproof); +44 snocm.  Kind 8: a body checked
\ against its header (sbody), the outputs it makes back at +24.
: cwon variable ;  : cwj variable ;  : cwjr variable ;  : cwjw variable ;  : cwvr variable ;  : cwvw variable ;
: cwk variable ;  : cwb variable ;  : cwm variable ;  : cwp1 variable ;  : cwp2 variable ;
\ cwcv: the bytes the verifier's buffers took on the node (main.fam
\ measures them): the worker's heap is that and 1 MiB (the state's
\ buffers, about 300 KiB, and its data stack).
: cwcv variable ;
\ cwinit  on the worker: its own buffers.
: cwinit
0 lit p2s !  0 lit dva !  0 lit mrb !  0 lit mcb !  0 lit pws !
10 lit alloc et1 !  10 lit alloc et2 !  10 lit alloc et3 !  10 lit alloc lgt !  10 lit alloc lgp !
pwtext @ pwlen @ powinit
cwj @ 10 lit + @ stin0
400 lit alloc pin !  40 lit alloc pcs !  40 lit alloc ppub !  40 lit alloc ptmp !  CC lit alloc ppar !
sninit  cvp @ cvinit ;
\ cwput ( kind -- )  a job to the worker (its memory set first).
: cwput  cwm @ !  cwjw @ cwm @ 4 lit write drop ;
\ cwait ( -- code )  the worker's verdict, the network and the API served
\ meanwhile (as vwait: not blocks' chunks or snapshots, pnest).
: cwait
cwvr @ pyfd !  0 lit pyrdy !  1 lit pnest !
begin pyrdy @ 0= while
	-1 lit pxw !  3B9ACA00 lit pwait drop  0 lit pxw !
	\ the peers kept (pings: a long job must not leave them unanswered,
	\ docs/TIMING_FIXES.md) and the API's long polls answered meanwhile
	pkeep
	stx @ vsav !  pxrdy @ if aaccept then  awake  vsav @ stx !
repeat
0 lit pyfd !  0 lit pyrdy !  0 lit pnest !
cwvr @ cwm @ 4 lit read 4 lit = if cwm @ @ else FFFFFFFE lit then ;
\ cwstart  the worker started (cwon), its heap the verifier's buffers
\ and 1 MiB.  Before taking any job it says whether every buffer was had
\ (alloc gives 0 when the heap is short, and nothing would notice until
\ the first store through it): if not, the node does the work itself.
: cwstart
0 lit cwon !
48 lit malloc cwj !  10 lit alloc cwk !  10 lit alloc cwb !  10 lit alloc cwm !
10 lit alloc cwp1 !  10 lit alloc cwp2 !
cwp1 @ pipe 0< 0=  cwp2 @ pipe 0< 0= and cwj @ 0= 0= and if
	cwp1 @ @ cwjr !  cwp1 @ 4 lit + @ cwjw !  cwp2 @ @ cwvr !  cwp2 @ 4 lit + @ cwvw !
	stfd @ cwj @ 10 lit + !
	ptcode[ drop
		cwinit
		\ every buffer had: the last ones made (cvinit's), and room left
		cvb @ 0= 0=  tsib @ 0= 0= and  dirty @ 0= 0= and  10000 lit alloc 0= 0= and
		dup if
			vrb @ if nhead "the worker: its heap " puts 0 lit alloc s10@ - A lit rshift u. " KiB used of " puts cwcv @ 100000 lit + A lit rshift u. " KiB" puts 0A lit putc then
		then
		cwb @ !  cwvw @ cwb @ 4 lit write drop
		cwb @ @ 0= if 0 lit texit then
		begin cwjr @ cwk @ 4 lit read 4 lit = while
			cwj @ 10 lit + @ stfd !
			cwk @ @
			dup 1 lit = if
				cwj @ C lit + @ sprchk !  cwj @ @ swk !  cwj @ 44 lit + @ snocm !
				cwj @ @ cwj @ 4 lit + @ cwj @ 8 lit + @ sconnect
				0 lit swk !  0 lit snocm !
				btb @ cwj @ 14 lit + !  bts @ cwj @ 18 lit + !  btp @ cwj @ 1C lit + !  btc @ cwj @ 20 lit + !
				bout @ cwj @ 28 lit + !  bnout @ cwj @ 2C lit + !  sfirst @ cwj @ 30 lit + !  sfirsth @ cwj @ 34 lit + !
			else dup 2 lit = if sundo 0 lit
			else dup 3 lit = if cwj @ @ cwj @ 4 lit + @ cwj @ 8 lit + @ snman  snr @ snn @ + cwj @ 24 lit + !
			else dup 5 lit = if cwj @ @ cwj @ 4 lit + @ cwj @ 8 lit + @ sverify
			else dup 6 lit = if cwj @ @ cwj @ 4 lit + @ cwj @ 8 lit + @ snpart
			else dup 7 lit = if cwj @ @ snfin
			else dup 8 lit = if cwj @ @ cwj @ 4 lit + @ cwj @ 8 lit + @ sbody cwj @ 24 lit + !
			else cwj @ @ cwj @ 4 lit + @ cwj @ 8 lit + @ cwj @ 38 lit + @ cwj @ 3C lit + @ cwj @ 40 lit + @ sbproof
			then then then then then then then
			nip
			cwb @ !  cwvw @ cwb @ 4 lit write drop
		repeat
	]tcode
	0 lit cwcv @ 100000 lit + pthread 0< 0= if
		\ its word: every buffer had, or not
		cwvr @ cwm @ 4 lit read 4 lit = if cwm @ @ cwon ! then
		cwon @ 0= vrb @ and if nhead "the worker could not have its buffers" puts 0A lit putc then
	then
then ;

\ nconf ( from -- flag )  hconf, the work checked by nodev.
: nconf
-1 lit swap  hbest
begin dup hheight 2 lit pick u< 0= over hheight and while
	vrb @ if nhead "the proof of work of header " puts dup hheight u. 0A lit putc then
	dup hparent @ he htarget  dup vpow 0= if rot drop 0 lit -rot then
	hparent @ he
repeat 2drop ;
\ nconnect ( e body n -- code )  sconnect for header entry e (its work and
\ id kept with it: swk), by the worker, which checks the proof too; with
\ none, here, the proof checked by nodev.  Connected: its event
\ (events.fam).
: nevb variable ;
: nconnect
2 lit pick nevb !
2 lit pick 20 lit + @ pacth !  2 lit pact !
cwon @ if
	cwj @ 8 lit + !  cwj @ 4 lit + !  cwj @ !
	sprchk @ cwj @ C lit + !  stfd @ cwj @ 10 lit + !  snocm @ cwj @ 44 lit + !
	1 lit cwput
	\ the next block fetched meanwhile, if the caller named it (npnx)
	\ (its fetch's time is its own: this block's, as nbrk shows it, kept)
	btf @ nsvt !  npfetch  nsvt @ btf !  2 lit pact !  cwj @ @ 20 lit + @ pacth !
	cwait
	cwj @ 14 lit + @ btb !  cwj @ 18 lit + @ bts !  cwj @ 1C lit + @ btp !  cwj @ 20 lit + @ btc !
	\ what the pool reads of the block (qconfs, qmvblk), as sconnect left it
	cwj @ @ bh !  cwj @ 28 lit + @ bout !  cwj @ 2C lit + @ bnout !  cwj @ 30 lit + @ sfirst !  cwj @ 34 lit + @ sfirsth !
else
	2 lit pick swk !  sconn1  spend @ if vproof else -1 lit then  sconn2  0 lit swk !
then
0 lit npnx !  0 lit pact !
dup 0= if EVBLK nevb @ hheight 0 lit nevb @ hid 0 lit evput then ;
\ cwjob ( a b c kind -- r )  a job of three arguments by the worker,
\ the node serving meanwhile.
: cwkd variable ;
: cwjob  cwkd !  cwj @ 8 lit + !  cwj @ 4 lit + !  cwj @ !  stfd @ cwj @ 10 lit + !  cwkd @ cwput cwait ;
\ The fast sync's snapshot, by the worker if there is one (nsnp: the
\ parts' count after the manifest).
: nsnp variable ;
: nsnman  cwon @ if 3 lit cwjob cwj @ 24 lit + @ nsnp ! else snman snr @ snn @ + nsnp ! then ;   \ ( m n hS -- code )
: nsver  cwon @ if 5 lit cwjob else sverify then ;          \ ( hS body n -- flag )
: nspart  cwon @ if 6 lit cwjob else snpart then ;         \ ( i p n -- code )
: nsfin  cwon @ if 0 lit 0 lit 7 lit cwjob else snfin then ;   \ ( hS -- code )
\ nundo  sundo, by the worker if there is one; its event (events.fam),
\ the tip's height and id before.
: nundo
EVUNDO myh @ 0 lit mytip @ 0 lit evput
cwon @ if stfd @ cwj @ 10 lit + !  2 lit cwput  cwait drop else sundo then ;

\ The blocks after our tip, by batches (docs/NODE_ENHANCEMENTS.md, item
\ 21): up to 16 at a time fetched (each from one of up to 16 peers taken
\ at random, those not seeds first) and their bodies checked against
\ their headers (nsbody: the commitment covers the chain proof too); then
\ only the last one's chain proof checked, before any is connected (it
\ attests the block and every one before it, and the work of every
\ header before it); then the batch connected without proofs, its
\ commitments not checked again.  The last block is held for the next
\ batch, whose proof covers its own work, but for the run's top (the best
\ header, its work checked in full).  A batch whose proof fails is
\ bisected (each proof attests all before it) to its first bad block:
\ those before it connected, and from it on each block connected as
\ before (its proof checked), so that a refusal is today's code's; the
\ block's sender banned.  A body that does not match its header: its
\ sender banned, the block asked of the next peer.
\ nrun ( top mode -- code )  from our tip to top: 0, 1 a block not had
\ (nrbad its height), or the code of the block refused at nrbad.  mode 1:
\ ncatch's bookkeeping for each block connected (ndone), 0 nsync's.
: nuw variable ;  : nchg variable ;  : ncn variable ;  : nln variable ;
: nq variable ;  : nqn variable ;  : nqa variable ;  : nqby variable ;  : ncl variable ;  : nch variable ;
: ntop variable ;  : nrbad variable ;  : nmode variable ;  : nrcd variable ;
: npl variable ;  : npc variable ;  : nrs variable ;  : nqk variable ;  : nqok variable ;  : nqsnd variable ;
: nsvk variable ;  : nqj variable ;  : nqt variable ;  : nqb variable ;  : nqg variable ;  : nqm variable ;
:M NQMAX 10 lit ;                       \ blocks a batch
:M NQBY 800000 lit ;                    \ bytes a batch holds at most (8 MiB)
\ A slot (14 bytes): the block (header and body, malloc'd), its length,
\ the output counter before it (lo, hi), the peer it came from.
: nqs  14 lit * nq @ + ;                 \ ( j -- a )
: nqh  nqa @ + ;                         \ ( j -- height )
\ nrnd ( n -- r )  0 to n-1, at random (xorshift).
: nrnd
nrs @ ?dup 0= if ticks pkey @ @ xor 1 lit or then
dup D lit lshift xor  dup 11 lit rshift xor  dup 5 lit lshift xor  dup nrs !
1 lit rshift swap % ;
\ npick ( h -- )  the batch's peers: those answering, not banned, at or
\ above height h, holding the batch's first block; shuffled, those not
\ seeds first, 16 at most; none: the current alone.
: npsh  ( from -- )  npc @ over - 1 lit u> if npc @ over - 1 lit - 0 lit do
	npc @ i - 1 lit -  ( from last )
	dup 2 lit pick - 1 lit + nrnd 2 lit pick +  ( from last r )
	2 lit lshift npl @ + swap 2 lit lshift npl @ + 2dup @ swap @ rot ! swap !
loop then drop ;
: npok  ( h k -- flag )
dup prec 8 lit + @  over prec B0 lit + @ 0= and  over pbanned 0= and
over nsil? 0= and  over prec C4 lit + @ secs swap - 0< 0= and
over prec 4C lit + @ 3 lit pick u< 0= and  swap prec 50 lit + @ nqa @ u> 0= and  nip ;
: npick
0 lit npc !
pnp @ ?dup if 0 lit do dup i npok  i pisseed 0= and  npc @ 10 lit u< and if i npl @ npc @ 2 lit lshift + !  npc @ 1 lit + npc ! then loop then
0 lit npsh  npc @ nqg !
pnp @ ?dup if 0 lit do dup i npok  i pisseed and  npc @ 10 lit u< and if i npl @ npc @ 2 lit lshift + !  npc @ 1 lit + npc ! then loop then
nqg @ npsh  drop
npc @ 0= if pcur @ npl @ !  1 lit npc ! then ;
: npeer  npc @ % 2 lit lshift npl @ + @ ;   \ ( j -- k )  slot j's first peer
\ nbfrom ( e k -- flag )  entry e's block from peer k into nblk/nbn (the
\ one fetched ahead if it is e's), nqsnd who sent it.
: nbfrom
over npe @ =  npb @ 0= 0= and if
	2drop  npb @ nblk !  npn @ nbn !  0 lit npb !  0 lit npe !  npks @ nqsnd !  -1 lit
else
	npdrop  dup nqsnd !  pcur @ nsvk !  puse  nblock  nsvk @ puse
then ;
\ nsbody ( h body n -- code n )  sbody by the worker, the next block
\ (npnx, from npk) fetched meanwhile.
: nsbody
cwon @ if
	cwj @ 8 lit + !  cwj @ 4 lit + !  cwj @ !  stfd @ cwj @ 10 lit + !  8 lit cwput
	btf @ nsvt !  npfetch  nsvt @ btf !
	cwait  cwj @ 24 lit + @
else sbody then ;
\ nsbpr ( j -- flag )  slot j's chain proof, before its parent is
\ connected (sbproof, by the worker).
: nsbpr
dup nqs nqt !  nqh dup pacth !  2 lit pact !
dup hat hhdr  nqt @ @ CC lit +  nqt @ 4 lit + @ CC lit -  nqt @ 8 lit + @  nqt @ C lit + @
5 lit pick 1 lit - hat hhdr
cwon @ if
	cwj @ 40 lit + !  cwj @ 3C lit + !  cwj @ 38 lit + !  cwj @ 8 lit + !  cwj @ 4 lit + !  cwj @ !  stfd @ cwj @ 10 lit + !
	9 lit cwput  cwait
else sbproof then
nip  0 lit pact ! ;
\ nqget ( j -- flag )  slot j fetched and its body checked: from its
\ peer, else the next, and so on; the next slot's block fetched while
\ the worker checks this one.  A body its header does not commit to: its
\ sender banned (a seed only passed over).
: nqget
nqj !  0 lit nqok !
npc @ 0 lit do nqok @ 0= if
	nqj @ i + npeer nqk !
	nqk @ nsil? 0= if
		nqj @ nqh hat nqk @ nbfrom dup 0= if nwhy @ 1 lit = if nqk @ nsil! then then
	else 0 lit then
	if
		nqj @ 1 lit + nqm @ u< if nqj @ 1 lit + nqh hat npnx !  nqj @ 1 lit + npeer 1 lit + npk ! then
		nqj @ nqh hat hhdr  nblk @ CC lit +  nbn @ CC lit -  nsbody
		swap ?dup if
			vrb @ if nhead "block " puts nqj @ nqh u. " from peer " puts nqsnd @ pshow " refused: " puts . "; asked of another" puts 0A lit putc else drop then
			drop  nqsnd @ pisseed 0= if nqsnd @ pban then  nblk @ free  0 lit nblk !
		else
			nqj @ nqs nqt !
			nblk @ nqt @ !  nbn @ nqt @ 4 lit + !  ncl @ nqt @ 8 lit + !  nch @ nqt @ C lit + !  nqsnd @ nqt @ 10 lit + !
			nqby @ nbn @ + nqby !  0 lit nblk !
			\ the counter after it (40 bits)
			ncl @ over + dup ncl @ u< if nch @ 1 lit + nch ! then ncl !  drop
			nqj @ 1 lit + nqn !  -1 lit nqok !
		then
	then
then loop
nqok @ ;
\ nqfill ( -- flag )  the batch's slots filled, from nqn to nqm, or fewer
\ once it holds NQBY bytes (nqm then cut to them).
: nqfill
-1 lit nqok !
begin nqok @ nqn @ nqm @ u< and while
	nqby @ NQBY u< 0= if nqn @ nqm ! else nqn @ nqget drop then
repeat
npdrop  nqok @ ;
\ ndone ( h -- )  block h connected: ncatch's bookkeeping (mode 1), our
\ status, the line.
: ndone
nstat
nmode @ if
	drop  nk @ 1 lit + nk !  1 lit nchg !  nuw @ if qmvblk then  qconfs  ncn @ 1 lit + ncn !  nbn @ nln !
	vrb @ if nhead "height " puts myh @ u. nbrk 0A lit putc then
else
	vrb @ if nhead "block " puts u. " of " puts ntop @ u. " connected" puts nbrk 0A lit putc else drop then
then ;
\ nqcon ( j proof -- code )  slot j connected (its proof checked if
\ proof is set; its commitment not again); freed if it was.
: nqcon
sprchk !  -1 lit snocm !  0 lit btf !
dup nqs nqt !  dup nqh hat hhdr  nqt @ @ CC lit +  nqt @ 4 lit + @ CC lit -  nconnect
0 lit snocm !  -1 lit sprchk !
dup 0= if
	nqt @ 4 lit + @ nbn !  over nqh ndone
	over nqs dup @ free  0 lit swap !
then nip ;
\ nqbyb ( j -- )  slots j to the batch's end connected as before, each
\ one's proof checked; one refused stops the run (nrcd, nrbad), its
\ sender banned.
: nqbyb
begin dup nqm @ u< nrcd @ 0= and while
	dup -1 lit nqcon ?dup if
		nrcd !  dup nqh nrbad !  dup nqs 10 lit + @ dup pisseed if drop else pban then
	else 1 lit + then
repeat drop
nrcd @ 0= if nqa @ nqm @ + nqa !  0 lit nqn !  0 lit nqby ! then ;
\ nqatt ( g -- ok )  slots 0 to g-1, attested, connected without their
\ proofs.  Not ok: one refused (a fault of ours: the proof passed on
\ other data), and the batch then connected by nqbyb from it.
: nqe variable ;
: nqatt
nqe !  0 lit nqj !  -1 lit nqok !
begin nqj @ nqe @ u< nqok @ and while
	nqj @ 0 lit nqcon ?dup if
		vrb @ if nhead "block " puts nqj @ nqh u. " refused though attested (" puts . "); the batch connected block by block" puts 0A lit putc else drop then
		0 lit nqok !  nqj @ nqbyb
	else nqj @ 1 lit + nqj ! then
repeat
nqok @ ;
\ nqshift  after slots 0 to nqgg-1: the last, if held, made slot 0.
: nqgg variable ;
: nqshift
nqgg @ nqm @ u< if
	nqm @ 1 lit - nqs nq @ 14 lit bcopy  0 lit nqm @ 1 lit - nqs !
	nqa @ nqm @ 1 lit - + nqa !  1 lit nqn !  nq @ 4 lit + @ nqby !
else nqa @ nqm @ + nqa !  0 lit nqn !  0 lit nqby ! then ;
\ nbatch  one batch: filled, its last proof checked, connected (or
\ bisected).
: nqtb variable ;
: nbatch
ntop @ nqa @ - 1 lit + NQMAX umin nqm !
nqm @ 1 lit - nqh npick
ticks nt0 !
nqfill 0= if
	nqn @ nqh nrbad !  1 lit nrcd !
else
	nqn @ nqm !  ticks nt0 @ - nqtb !  ticks nt0 !
	nqm @ 1 lit - nsbpr
	vrb @ if
		nhead "blocks " puts nqa @ u. " to " puts nqm @ 1 lit - nqh u. ": fetched and checked in " puts nqtb @ nsec
		" s, the last one's proof in " puts ticks nt0 @ - nsec " s" puts 0A lit putc
	then
	if
		\ attested: connected, the last held for the next batch's proof
		\ (its own work) but at the top (its work checked in full)
		nqm @ 1 lit - nqh ntop @ = if nqm @ else nqm @ 1 lit - then  1 lit max  nqgg !
		nqgg @ nqatt if nqshift then
	else
		\ a bad block in it: the first, by bisection (good, bad: slots)
		-1 lit nqg !  nqm @ 1 lit - nqb !
		begin nqb @ nqg @ - 1 lit > while
			nqg @ nqb @ + 2 lit /  dup nsbpr if nqg ! else nqb ! then
		repeat
		vrb @ if nhead "the batch's proof failed; the first bad block by its proof: " puts nqb @ nqh u. 0A lit putc then
		nqb @ nqatt if nqb @ nqbyb then
		nrcd @ 0= vrb @ and if nhead "the batch's proof failed, but each of its blocks' passed" puts 0A lit putc then
	then
then ;
\ nqclr  the batch's blocks left freed.
: nqclr  NQMAX 0 lit do i nqs @ ?dup if free then  0 lit i nqs ! loop  0 lit nqn !  npdrop ;
: nrun  ( top mode -- code )
nmode !  ntop !  0 lit nrcd !  0 lit nrbad !  0 lit nsil !
nstat  myh @ 1 lit + nqa !  0 lit nqn !  0 lit nqby !
stfd @ 0 lit txbegin stx !  70 lit mget ncl !  71 lit mget nch !  stx @ txcommit drop
begin nqa @ ntop @ u> 0= nrcd @ 0= and while nbatch repeat
nqclr  nrcd @ ;

\ nsave ( n -- )  the main chain's headers 1 to n held into the store,
\ with their work (a transaction a 1,024): after a fast sync's snapshot,
\ so that the store holds every header from genesis to its tip (sconnect
\ stores each block's after; ncompact those dropped before), for a start
\ to load (nload) and for peers asking for old headers.
\ ncompact  when the headers held near their room (hcap), the main
\ chain's below a height saved in the store and dropped (hprune): the
\ newest half kept, and never above our tip less 8 (where a fork is
\ found from) or, before any block is connected, the best less 160 (a
\ fast sync's S and the blocks after it).  nkeep, if set, how many to
\ keep (main.fam's -w), else half the room.
: nsv variable ;
: nsave
nsv !  1 lit
begin dup nsv @ u> 0= while
	stfd @ 1 lit txbegin stx !
	dup 400 lit + nsv @ 1 lit + umin  over do
		i hat ?dup if  i khdr over hhdr CC lit sput  shidx  then
	loop
	stx @ txcommit drop
	400 lit +
repeat drop ;

\ ncompact
: nkeep variable ;  : ncf variable ;
: ncompact
hcnt @  hcap @ 80 lit hcap @ 2 lit rshift umin -  u< 0= if
	hbest hheight  nkeep @ ?dup 0= if hcap @ 1 lit rshift then  -
	myh @ if myh @ 8 lit - else hbest hheight A0 lit - then  2dup u> if swap then drop   \ the lesser
	dup 0< over 2 lit u< or over hbase @ u> 0= or if drop else
		ncf !
		hbase @ 2 lit max
		begin dup ncf @ u< while
			stfd @ 1 lit txbegin stx !
			dup 400 lit + ncf @ umin  over do
				i hat ?dup if  i khdr over hhdr CC lit sput  shidx  then
			loop
			stx @ txcommit drop
			400 lit +
		repeat drop
		ncf @ hprune
		vrb @ if nhead "headers below " puts ncf @ u. " now only in the store (" puts hcnt @ u. " held)" puts 0A lit putc then
	then
then ;

\ nload ( -- flag )  the store's chain taken up, if it has one: its last
\ nldn headers (2,048 if not set) to its tip, trusted (each was checked in
\ full, or covered by a proof, before it was stored: htrust, only how
\ each joins checked), the first a root (hroot, its work the store's)
\ after block 1 (ASERT's anchor), or all from block 1 if fewer; and our
\ status from its tip.  0 if the store has no tip, or a header is
\ missing or does not join.
: nlh variable ;  : nlok variable ;  : nlb variable ;  : nldn variable ;
: nlone  ntime 0 lit hacc 1 lit u> if 0 lit nlok ! then ;   \ ( h -- )  a header taken up
: nload
stfd @ 0 lit txbegin stx !  68 lit mget nlh !  stx @ txcommit drop
nlh @ 0= 0= nlok !
nlok @ if
	nldn @ ?dup 0= if 800 lit then  nlh @ over u> if nlh @ swap - 1 lit + else drop 1 lit then  nlb !
	vrb @ if nhead "loading " puts nlh @ nlb @ - 1 lit + u. " headers from the store" puts 0A lit putc then
	ticks nt0 !  -1 lit htrust !
	nlb @ 1 lit u> if
		1 lit yentry ?dup if nlone  hcnt @ 1 lit - hb1 ! else 0 lit nlok ! then
		nlok @ if nlb @ yentry ?dup if dup hwork hroot  nlb @ hbase ! else 0 lit nlok ! then then
	then
	stfd @ 0 lit txbegin stx !
	nlh @ 1 lit +  nlb @ 1 lit u> if nlb @ 1 lit + else 1 lit then
	2dup u> if do
		nlok @ if i khdr sbuf @ CC lit sget CC lit = if sbuf @ nlone else 0 lit nlok ! then then
	loop else 2drop then
	stx @ txcommit drop
	0 lit htrust !
	nlok @ hbest hheight nlh @ = and nlok !
then
nlok @ if nstat  -1 lit sprchk !  vrb @ if nhead "resumed at height " puts myh @ u. ", the headers loaded in " puts ticks nt0 @ - nsec " s" puts 0A lit putc then then
nlok @ ;

\ nswr: set once nsync has begun writing the store (the snapshot's parts),
\ so a sync that stops after must start again on a fresh tree.
: nswr variable ;
: nsync  ( depth -- code )
nS !  0 lit ncode !  0 lit nswr !
pping 0= if FFFFFFFF lit nfail else "the peer is at height " nsay pst-h nsayn then
\ a chain with no block yet: nothing to sync from (-10; asked again later)
ncode @ 0= pst-h 0= and if FFFFFFF6 lit nfail then
ncode @ 0= if pst @ 14 lit + mygen @ 20 lit d8= 0= if FFFFFFFE lit nfail then then
\ headers, quick-checked
ncode @ 0= if
	-1 lit hquick !  1 lit
	begin dup pst-h u> 0= ncode @ 0= and while
		ncompact  dup phdrs ?dup if
			0 lit do phb @ i CC lit * +  ntime 0 lit hacc  1 lit u> if FFFFFFFD lit nfail then loop
			hbest hheight 1 lit + max
			"headers to " nsay hbest hheight nsayn
		else FFFFFFFD lit nfail then
	repeat drop
	0 lit hquick !
then
\ S, and the full proof of work from it up
ncode @ 0= if
	hbest hheight dup nH !  nS @ - dup 1 lit < if drop 1 lit then nS !
	"fast sync from block S = " nsay nS @ nsayn
	ticks nt0 !
	nH @ nconf 0= if FFFFFFFC lit nfail else vrb @ if nhead "its work checked in " puts ticks nt0 @ - nsec " s" puts 0A lit putc then then
then
\ S's block and manifest, its parent's header, its proof
ncode @ 0= if
	nS @ hat dup nblock 0= if drop FFFFFFFB lit nfail else
		hid nid !
		2 lit 0 lit nid @ nfetch ?dup if
			nS @ hat hhdr nsnman if FFFFFFF8 lit nfail then
		else drop FFFFFFFB lit nfail then
	then
then
ncode @ 0= if
	"S's block and its snapshot's manifest fetched; checking its chain proof" nsay vrb @ if 0A lit putc then
	nS @ 1 lit - hat hhdr shdr
	nS @ hat hhdr  nblk @ CC lit +  nbn @ CC lit -  nsver 0= if FFFFFFFA lit nfail else
		"S's chain proof checked (it covers every block before S); snapshot parts: " nsay nsnp @ nsayn
	then
then
\ the parts, then the whole
ncode @ 0= if
	1 lit nswr !
	nsnp @ ?dup if 0 lit do
		ncode @ 0= if
			3 lit i nid @ nfetch over if
				2dup i -rot nspart if FFFFFFF9 lit nfail else "snapshot part " nsay i 1 lit + nsayn then drop free
			else 2drop FFFFFFFB lit nfail then
		then
	loop then
then
\ (the headers to S saved first: once snfin sets the tip, a start finds
\ them all)
ncode @ 0= if nS @ nsave  nS @ hat hhdr nsfin if FFFFFFF8 lit nfail else "the snapshot's state checked against S" nsay vrb @ if 0A lit putc then then then
nblk @ ?dup if free 0 lit nblk ! then
\ the blocks after S, by batches (nrun)
ncode @ 0= if
	-1 lit sprchk !  nstat
	nH @ nS @ u> if
		nH @ 0 lit nrun ?dup if
			1 lit = if FFFFFFFB lit nfail else FFFFFFF7 lit nfail then
			vrb @ if nhead "stopped at block " puts nrbad @ u. 0A lit putc then
		then
	then
	nstat
then
ncode @ ;

\ ncatch  headers from the best to the peer's height, each quick-checked
\ and the best's work then in full (as a fast sync: each other's is
\ covered by the proof of the block after it, checked as it connects; a
\ best whose work fails is set aside): asked for from the best's height on, or, when the first of them
\ does not join (its parent unknown: the peer's chain forked below our
\ best), from 2, 4, 8... lower until it does.  Then, if our tip is not on
\ the best branch, our blocks above where it joins undone (sundo: there
\ is undo data for every block connected, none for a fast sync's S and
\ below, so no deeper); then every block from our tip to the best header
\ connected.  A block refused sets its header aside (hmark), so the best
\ is another branch, ours or the old: the next turn goes back to it.  nk
\ counts the blocks connected.
: nfl variable ;  : nhb variable ;  : nstp variable ;  : nbk variable ;  : nfk variable ;  : nb0 variable ;  : nrl variable ;
\ nann  our tip announced (Inv: its header and its block's length) to
\ every answering peer but the current, as tabminer relays a block it
\ accepts: only ever the best header, whose work is checked in full
\ before it is the best; a peer that wants it asks for its chunks (pgive).
: nann
0 lit nrl !
pnp @ ?dup if 0 lit do
	i pcur @ <>  i prec 8 lit + @ and  i prec B0 lit + @ 0= and  i pbanned 0= and if
		7 lit wbeg  myh @ hat hhdr CC lit wbs  nln @ w32  i psend  nrl @ 1 lit + nrl !
	then
loop then
vrb @ nrl @ and if nhead "block " puts myh @ u. " relayed to " puts nrl @ u. " peers" puts 0A lit putc then ;
\ nundo? ( -- flag )  undo data for our tip's block.
: nundo?  stfd @ 0 lit txbegin stx !  myh @ 0 lit kundo sbuf @ 4 lit sget 0 lit >  stx @ txcommit drop ;
: ncatch
0 lit nfl !  ticks nt0 !  hbest hheight nh0 !  1 lit nstp !  0 lit nuw !  0 lit nchg !  qmvoff
hbst @ nb0 !  0 lit ncn !  -1 lit hquick !
begin hbest hheight pst-h u< nfl @ 0= and while
	hbest hheight 1 lit +  nstp @ 1 lit -  over 1 lit - umin  -
	0 lit nbk !
	ncompact  dup phdrs ?dup if
		0 lit do nfl @ 0= nbk @ 0= and if
			phb @ i CC lit * + ntime 0 lit hacc
			dup FFFFFFFE lit = i 0= and if
				drop  1 lit nbk !
				dup 1 lit = if 1 lit nfl ! else nstp @ 1 lit lshift nstp ! then
			else
				\ refused: the peer struck, but for a timestamp ahead of our
				\ clock, a branch set aside, or our room
				dup 1 lit u> if
					dup FFFFFFFA lit <> over FFFFFFF7 lit <> and over FFFFFFF8 lit <> and if pcur @ pstrike then
					1 lit nfl !
				then drop
			then
		then loop
	else 1 lit nfl ! then
	drop
repeat
0 lit hquick !
\ the best's work in full; one that fails set aside, until one passes
hbst @ nb0 @ <> if
	begin hbst @ nb0 @ <> if hbest hheight nconf 0= else 0 lit then while
		vrb @ if nhead "header " puts hbest hheight u. "'s proof of work refused; its branch set aside" puts 0A lit putc then
		hbest hmark  pcur @ pstrike
	repeat
	vrb @ if
		nhead "headers to " puts hbest hheight u. ", fetched and the best's work checked in " puts ticks nt0 @ - nsec " s" puts 0A lit putc
	then
then
0 lit nfl !
\ our tip off the best branch: undone down to where it joins
myh @ if mytip @ hfind dup 0< if drop else
	he begin dup dup hheight hat <> over hparent @ 0< 0= and while hparent @ he repeat
	dup dup hheight hat = if hheight nfk ! else
		\ the fork below the headers held (a root reached): not followed
		drop  myh @ nfk !  1 lit nfl !
		vrb @ if nhead "the best branch forks below the headers held: not followed" puts 0A lit putc then
	then
	myh @ nfk @ u> if
		vrb @ if nhead "reorganizing: our " puts myh @ nfk @ - u. " blocks above " puts nfk @ u. " leave for the best branch" puts 0A lit putc then
		begin myh @ nfk @ u> nfl @ 0= and while
			nundo? if nundo nstat  1 lit nuw !  1 lit nchg !  vrb @ if nhead "undone to height " puts myh @ u. 0A lit putc then
			else
				vrb @ if nhead "cannot undo block " puts myh @ u. " (none is kept for a fast sync's start and below): a new sync is needed" puts 0A lit putc then
				1 lit nfl !
			then
		repeat
	then
then then
myh @ hbest hheight u< nfl @ 0= and if
	hbest hheight 1 lit nrun ?dup if
		dup 1 lit = if
			drop vrb @ if nhead "block not fetched: " puts nrbad @ u. nwhy. 0A lit putc then
		else
			vrb @ if nhead "block " puts nrbad @ u. " refused: " puts dup . "; its branch set aside" puts 0A lit putc then
			\ a chain proof that fails on a block with a full proof of work
			\ behind it is deliberate: the headers' peer banned at once
			FFFFFFEF lit = if pcur @ pban else pcur @ pstrike then
			nrbad @ hat hmark
		then
		1 lit nfl !
	then
then
\ the pool: out what the new blocks spent or settled otherwise, onto the
\ shelf; back from the shelf what is valid again (the blocks undone)
nchg @ if
	0 lit qout !  ticks nt0 !  qcheck qreturn
	vrb @ qnum @ qout @ or qbk @ or and if
		nhead "the pool: " puts qnum @ u. " held, " puts qout @ u. " out (mined or conflicted), " puts qbk @ u. " back; in " puts
		ticks nt0 @ - nsec " s" puts 0A lit putc
	then
	qmvoff
then
ncn @ myh @ hbest hheight = and if nann then ;

\ pfollow ( n -- k )  each announcement (Inv) taken as the peer's height,
\ and caught up to; up to a minute a block.
: pfollow
0 lit nk !
dup 3C lit * 0 lit do
	nk @ over u< if
		3B9ACA00 lit pwait 7 lit = if  prx @ 25 lit + le@ pst @ 34 lit + !  ncatch  then
	then
loop drop nk @ ;

: nrid variable ;  : nrk variable ;  : nrm variable ;  : nrc variable ;
: nrelay
begin pdeq ?dup while
	dup nrid @ 20 lit bcopy  20 lit + @ nrk !
	nrid @ nrm @ dle  nrm @ qfind 0< if
		pcur @ nrc !  nrk @ puse  1 lit 0 lit nrid @ nfetch  nrc @ puse
		?dup if
			2dup qadmit  "pool: " puts dup . 20 lit putc nrid @ nhex 0A lit putc
			dup FFFFFFFF lit = if nrk @ pstrike then   \ bytes that do not decode
			0= if nrid @ nrk @ pann then
			drop free
		else drop then
	then
repeat ;

\ nstep  a turn of following, up to a second: the peers kept (pkeep);
\ the answering peer furthest ahead of us, by its last Pong or
\ announcement (Inv), made the current and caught up to (so a block
\ announced while we were lost to it is not missed, and a peer gone is
\ replaced by another); one whose claim brought nothing passed over for
\ a minute; the transactions announced relayed.
: nah variable ;  : nahh variable ;
\ nahead ( -- k | -1 )
: nahead
FFFFFFFF lit nah !  myh @ nahh !
pnp @ ?dup if 0 lit do
	i prec 8 lit + @  i prec B0 lit + @ 0= and  secs i prec C4 lit + @ - 0< 0= and  i pbanned 0= and if
		i prec 4C lit + @ nahh @ u> if i nah !  i prec 4C lit + @ nahh ! then
	then
loop then nah @ ;
\ nrean  every pooled transaction announced again to every answering peer,
\ each minute: a peer that missed the first (silent then, restarted, a
\ datagram lost) asks for it now; one that has it does nothing.
: nrat variable ;
: nrc2 variable ;
: nrean
pfresh @ if 0 lit nrat !  0 lit pfresh ! then
secs nrat @ u< 0= if
	secs 3C lit + nrat !  0 lit nrc2 !
	QSLOTS 0 lit do i qused if i qslot 10 lit + nrm @ ycanon  nrm @ FFFFFFFF lit pann  nrc2 @ 1 lit + nrc2 ! then loop
	vrb @ nrc2 @ and if
		nhead "the pool's " puts nrc2 @ u. " transactions announced again, to " puts pnann @ u. " peers" puts 0A lit putc
	then
then ;
\ nnext ( -- ns )  nstep's wait (docs/TIMING_FIXES.md, item 16): to the
\ first thing due, not a fixed second: a peer's ping (A4), the end of its
\ pass-over (C4) or ban (B4), discovery (pdn), the pool announced again
\ (nrat), the message layer's check (cxat and 10 s), a waiting API
\ request's end; a second at least (the clock's unit, as before) and 4
\ at most (a wait is one word of nanoseconds; what this misses is that
\ late at most).  A datagram or the API wakes it sooner.
: nnx variable ;  : nnow variable ;
\ nnmin ( s -- )  s, unless past, the first due if before the others.
: nnmin  dup nnow @ - 0< if drop else dup nnx @ - 0< if nnx ! else drop then then ;
: nnext
secs nnow !  nnow @ 4 lit + nnx !
pnp @ ?dup if 0 lit do
	i prec A4 lit + @ nnmin  i prec C4 lit + @ nnmin  i prec B4 lit + @ nnmin
loop then
pdn @ nnmin  nrat @ nnmin  cxat @ A lit + nnmin
\ (the API's tables only once ainit made them: a node's test program
\ without the API, relay_test, read address 0 here and was killed)
aew @ if AEW 0 lit do aew @ i AEWSZ * + dup @ if 4 lit + @ nnmin else drop then loop then
awt @ if 8 lit 0 lit do awt @ i 28 lit * + dup @ if 4 lit + @ nnmin else drop then loop then
nnx @ nnow @ -  dup 1 lit u< if drop 1 lit then  3B9ACA00 lit * ;
: nstep
-1 lit pxw !  nnext pwait drop  0 lit pxw !
pkeep
nahead dup 0< if drop else
	dup pcur @ <> if dup puse  vrb @ if nhead "following peer " puts dup pshow 0A lit putc then then drop
	ncatch
	nchg @ 0= if
		\ (its own field: B4 is the ban's, which this must not shorten;
		\ a minute, not tabminer's ten: the node often has one or two
		\ peers, and passing over its only one would stall it)
		secs 3C lit + pcur @ prec C4 lit + !
		vrb @ if nhead "peer " puts pcur @ pshow " brought nothing to its height " puts pst-h u. "; passed over for a minute" puts 0A lit putc then
	then
then
nrelay  nrean  qpersist  cxrun ;

\ nserve ( s -- )
: nserve  0 lit do nstep loop ;

: ninit  NQMAX 14 lit * alloc dup nq ! NQMAX 5 lit * wzero  40 lit alloc npl !  40 lit alloc nbuf !  E0 lit alloc nhb !  0 lit nblk !  20 lit alloc nrid !  20 lit alloc nrm ! ;

\ aserve ( s -- )  (api.fam's)
: aserve
secs + aend !
begin secs aend @ u< while
	nstep
	aaccept
	awake
repeat ;
